# Dragon Cliffs Map (biome: dragon_cliffs)
# Symbols (assets/tiles.yaml, dragon_cliffs biome):
#   . = cliff grass   V = scorched basalt   S = cold stream   H = heather (walk)
#   M = bridge v0   N = bridge v1   E = chasm edge v0   J = chasm edge v1
#   C = chasm bottom v0   F = chasm bottom v1 (impassable pits)
#   % = cliff wall   # = basalt wall   B = ruin wall   = = slate wall
#   T = wind pine   A = rock outcrop   R = boulder   D = dragon bones (solid)
#   W = tarn water   Q = deep tarn (impassable without Walk on Water)
#   + = start   @ = bound NPC/stile (see >[...])
# Monster spawns: e = dragon_green  y = dragon_gold  v = mountain_troll  z = archmage
#
# Built the way the Xeen surface is built: one continuous mountain RING with
# named passes encloses the heart of the plateau (the way the Gemstone Range
# rings the Desert of Doom), the interior stays open with a few island crags,
# and the dragon country is four separate nests, not one heap.
#
# NORTH OF THE CHASM
#   The Coldspring strip (x1-8): the shrine of the spring (A-ring, a tome) at
#     the top, the cold stream running its whole length, cliff spurs off the
#     west wall, trolls; the crevice hoard at (1,12) is a dead end with iron.
#   THE WARDEN RING (x10-27, y2-13): an unbroken cliff chain around the Green
#     Basin. Two passes: the WINDGATE (west, enter at (11,4), weave south round
#     the inner spur at x12-13) and the BASIN GATE (south wall, x18-19, with an
#     outer spur below it). The ring can also simply be walked AROUND along the
#     top of the map - it guards the basin, not the region.
#   The Green Basin (inside the ring): the slate WARDEN VAULT (x16-21, y6-9),
#     steel door south, a golden hoard inside; archmages walk the basin.
#   THE EMBER BURN (x28-43): basalt. Four nests - the CINDER SHELF along the
#     top (a gold in the pocket at (31,2)), the BONE LAIR ruin (x35-40, gate at
#     (37,5)), the BONE FIELD (dragon bones on open basalt, x30-34 y9-11), and
#     the EMBER CRATER (x37-41 y9-13, gate south at (39,13)). The basalt vent
#     lane at x41 (y2-7) is a reserved dead end for a future secret.
#
# THE DRAGONMAW - the chasm crosses the whole map in three sheared steps, NE
#   high to SW low. The RANGER SPAN (x9-10) carries the camp road north; the
#   OLD SPAN (x39) is one plank between ruined abutments and lands you at the
#   crater's gate.
#
# SOUTH OF THE CHASM
#   Coldbrook Camp (x1-11): pine palisade with a north gate at x8-9 onto the
#     span road; tavern, ranger, the start, the violet teleporter, two caches.
#   The Long Moor: open heather; the HERMIT'S CAIRN ring at (19-21, y25-27),
#     cairn boulders, a troll prowling the east cairns.
#   The DROWNED TARN (x33-41): black water in a jagged bowl, two bays biting
#     north-west, one islet.
#
# CAPABILITY GATES - rewards only, never a route; Fly clears both.
# gate: jump (26,17) spell_lectern - THE PINNACLE, a stack standing in the
#   chasm itself: from the north rim at (26,15) vault the pit, and again south
# gate: water (37,25) chest_golden - the tarn islet, wants Walk on Water
#   Hiding pockets (walk-in, one mouth): the moor horseshoe (28,24), the vault
#   forecourt behind the twin boulders (16-17,5), the bone scatter (36-38,7-8).
#   SCENES: THE FALLEN WYRM (x28-38, y7-11) - one dead dragon, skull west,
#   ribs east, the living greens nesting in its cage; TWIN SENTINELS (8/11,21)
#   flanking the span road; THE JETTY (33-34,27) - planks into the tarn that
#   stop; a WAYSTONE (26-28,1) stone-heather-stone, reserved for a future
#   cross-map thread.
